      "body": "# What does this PR do?\r\n\r\nFixes # (issue)\r\n\r\nAdds Intel GPU support to three observability features that currently only handle CUDA and NPU:\r\n\r\n- `enable_torch_profiler`: also record XPU activity. Today the trace on Intel GPU has CPU ops only.\r\n- `profile_modules`: use `torch.xpu.Event` on XPU. Today it is disabled with \"no supported accelerator\".\r\n- `llamafactory-cli env`: print XPU type, number, memory and driver version.\r\n\r\n### Changes\r\n\r\n- `src/llamafactory/train/callbacks.py`: add `ProfilerActivity.XPU` and the XPU event/synchronize functions.\r\n- `src/llamafactory/extras/env.py`: add an XPU section, mirroring the CUDA one.\r\n- `tests/train/test_callbacks.py`: new tests for the three features.\r\n\r\n### Testing\r\n\r\n**Intel Arc Pro B60** (torch 2.14.0+xpu, transformers 5.8.0)\r\n\r\n- New tests: 3 passed\r\n- Full suite: 345 passed (`main`'s 342 plus the 3 new tests)\r\n- Profiler trace from a LoRA SFT run now includes XPU activity: 1,629 kernel events\r\n\r\n**NVIDIA A100 80GB** (torch 2.13.0+cu130, transformers 5.8.0)\r\n\r\n- New tests: 3 passed\r\n\r\n\r\n## Before submitting\r\n\r\n- [x] Did you read the [contributor guideline](https://github.com/hiyouga/LLaMA-Factory/blob/main/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md)?\r\n- [x] Did you write any new necessary tests?",
